<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-3522] String &quot;defaultValue&quot; (instead of boolean) in some &quot;interpreter-settings.json&quot; files</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-3522</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;The&#160;&lt;em&gt;interpreter-settings.json&lt;/em&gt;&#160;file for each interpreter has details of each configurable parameter for that interpreter. Each parameter also has a&#160;&lt;em&gt;defaultValue&lt;/em&gt; setting.&#160;For boolean-typed parameters the &lt;em&gt;defaultValue&lt;/em&gt; must be set to &lt;em&gt;true&lt;/em&gt; or &lt;em&gt;false&lt;/em&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&#160;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;But in some of these&#160;&lt;em&gt;interpreter-settings.json&lt;/em&gt;&#160;files, the&#160;&lt;em&gt;defaultValue&lt;/em&gt;&#160;has been set to the string values&#160;&lt;em&gt;&quot;true&quot;&lt;/em&gt;&#160;and&#160;&lt;em&gt;&quot;false&quot;&lt;/em&gt;&#160;(the quote marks are included in the value provided).&#160;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
